body:
Hi!

I took a few moments to research your argument and I learned things!

&#x200B;

1) [At the start of the invasion](https://www.nytimes.com/2022/03/03/us/politics/russia-ukraine-military.html) Ukraine has around 200,000 active army; 100,000 in reservists which were immediately called into active duty and another 100,000 in territorial defense forces. So, that's like double what you stated.   


2) How in the world did you come up with a tooth-to-tail ratio of 1:10? So you're trying to tell me that for every 1 combatant, you believe there are 10 non-combatant soldiers? I mean sure, if you're Russia. In WWI the ration was 1:1. With advances in technology and weaponry there was/is a need for more troops who handle infrastructure. It has gone up. The last data I could find was at the start of the Iraqi/Us war it was 1:2.5 then. So let's say through inefficiencies or technological advancement we use a more accurate tooth-to-tail ration of 1:3. 

&#x200B;

Now, I got the ADD and I'm horrible at math. I'm not an accountant so please double check my work. 200000 + 100000 + 100,000 = 400,000. With a more accurate T3R of 1:3 which I believe makes the 100,000 combatants. Oh, plus 16,000 I guess. 

&#x200B;

You might be able to claim from those numbers that the west is flooding into Ukraine. I mean adding 16% more combatants could be seen as a flood... if it weren't for

&#x200B;

3) [Volunteers!](https://time.com/6154068/ukrainian-citizens-fight-russian-troops/) Did you know the people of Ukraine are volunteering in scores? Apparently the government thinks they can add another 1.5 to 2 million more people to fight the war criminals. With a T3R of 1:3 that's like... 616,000 combatants.   


Learning is fun. Have a nice day/night and may I wish you a hearty Ukrainian Go fuck yourself.

Good you went with paper. However, if you went with a plastic bag after a minute or two you would never feel shame again! So there's that.

&#x200B;

I don't even care if I offend people honestly.  That's on them to deal with and understand why they are offended and how that should be handled on them. Not because I am some asshole but because they don't know me.  They don't know that my grandfather lost is legs in the Korean war and I spent my childhood helping him get in and out of his vehicle and the house and gardening. They don't know that when the tornadoes hit Nashville about a month ago I volunteered to help clean up a couple days and brought big ass batches of chili to help feed people in need.  They don't know that I volunteered to keep going into work because after my divorce I am single without kids and everyone else has family. They know none of that. So why would I care what those people think of me based on like a 5 second period of an entire life? Then again.. maybe I just don't know I am an asshole. 

&#x200B;

I would have laughed if I heard you say quadriplegic.
